  "bodyTypst": "A function $f$ has derivatives of all orders at $x = 0$. Let $P_(n)(x)$ denote the $n$ th-degree Taylor polynomial for $f$ about $x = 0$.\n\n(a) It is known that $f(0)= - 4$ and that $P_(1)lr((frac(1,2)))= - 3$. Show that $f'(0)= 2$.\n\n(b) It is known that $f''(0)= - frac(2,3)$ and $f'''(0)= frac(1,3)$. Find $P_(3)(x)$.\n\n(c) The function $h$ has first derivative given by $h'(x)= f(2 x)$. It is known that $h(0)= 7$. Find the third-degree Taylor polynomial for $h$ about $x = 0$.",
